diff --git a/examples/BOSCAMEFPGA/hello/README.md b/examples/BOSCAMEFPGA/hello/README.md
index 2140e722..e06a3ae8 100644
--- a/examples/BOSCAMEFPGA/hello/README.md
+++ b/examples/BOSCAMEFPGA/hello/README.md
@@ -59,6 +59,24 @@ Success is `verify hello: PASS` on stdout (full text under
 [Expected output](#expected-output)). Exit code 0 means load and capture
 succeeded; confirm PASS on the UART stream.
 
+### Scheduler completion and build overrides
+
+The single-hart runtime offers weak `bare_runtime_report_start()`,
+`bare_runtime_report_exit(int)`, and `bare_runtime_report_trap(...)` hooks.
+A scheduler transport can provide strong definitions in an extra object.
+The runtime preserves `main()`'s return value and reports it after
+`bare_runtime_after_main()` finishes; a fatal trap uses the separate trap hook.
+The default hooks emit no additional output.
+
+The makefile accepts `BUILD_DIR`, `EXTRA_OBJECTS`, `EXTRA_CFLAGS`, and
+`EXTRA_LDFLAGS` for a separate instrumented build. `UART_FREQ_HZ` defaults
+to 14745600; changing it alone does not change the historical UART driver's
+fixed divisor. For a 5.5296 MHz board, also set `UART_C` to the configurable
+driver at `runtime/boscame/uart/uart.c`, using an absolute path or a path
+relative to this example. The scheduling repository's build helper sets both
+and links its UART completion transport. This keeps the numerical check
+bit for bit identical; a failed check now returns 1 instead of 0.
+
 ## Files
 
 ```text
